steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1788287627
      nanos: 44280000
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_SYSTEM
    completed_at {
      seconds: 1788287627
      nanos: 44280000
    }
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "User prompt: Build a real-time CTG monitoring demo system extending the existing \nmodel (models/family_b_gradient_boosting.joblib) and FastAPI backend \n(src/app.py). This is a hackathon prototype simulating a hospital \nworkflow \342\200\224 not a real clinical deployment.\n\n=== DESIGN SYSTEM ===\n\nTwo visual modes in the same app:\n\nA) DASHBOARD SHELL (ward overview, patient list, forms, settings)\n   - Light theme: white/off-white backgrounds (#FAFAFA), soft card \n     shadows, thin borders\n   - Primary accent: royal blue (#0055FF)\n   - Heading text: near-black (#0B0B14), body text: dark gray (#4B4B55)\n   - Fonts: \"Plus Jakarta Sans\" for all UI text and body copy; \n     \"Instrument Serif\" (italic) for hero headings/emphasis words only, \n     matching a serif-italic-accent + clean-sans pairing\n   - Buttons: solid royal blue fill, white text, rounded corners\n\nB) LIVE WAVEFORM MONITOR PANEL (per-patient live view \342\200\224 this is the \n   hero component)\n   - Dark theme, isolated to this panel only: near-black background \n     (#0A0A0F), subtle grid lines like an oscilloscope\n   - Font: monospace throughout (IBM Plex Mono or JetBrains Mono), \n     all-caps labels\n   - FHR (fetal heart rate) trace color changes live with current \n     classification: mint green (#34D399) = Normal, amber (#F5A623) \n     = Suspect, red (#F04438) = Pathological\n   - UC (uterine contraction) trace: fixed violet (#A78BFA), \n     independent of classification\n   - Classification shown as pill badges at top (shield-check icon \n     for Normal, warning-triangle for Suspect, bolt icon for \n     Pathological), active one highlighted in its color\n   - Live readout box: current bpm, ASTV %, and a one-line morphology \n     description (e.g. \"Reduced variability & early decelerations\")\n   - Trace scrolls left-to-right in real time like a live monitor, \n     fed directly from the CTG Data Simulator / feature stream below\n\n=== 1. CTG DATA SIMULATOR ===\n   - Standalone service streaming synthetic FHR + UC signal over \n     WebSocket at realistic sampling rates, feeding both the feature \n     extraction pipeline AND the live waveform panel\'s animation\n   - 3 patient trajectories: stable/Normal, drifting toward Suspect, \n     acute Pathological event\n   - Multiple simultaneous simulated patients/beds\n\n=== 2. FEATURE EXTRACTION SERVICE ===\n   - Rolling window (e.g. 5 min) over the raw stream, computes the \n     21 CTG features the model expects (reference EXPLAINABILITY.md)\n   - Time-constrained fallback allowed: simulate pre-aggregated \n     feature vectors directly, clearly labeled as a scoped shortcut\n\n=== 3. REAL-TIME INFERENCE LOOP ===\n   - Runs the existing model on each new feature vector, per patient, \n     maintains per-patient state/history\n\n=== 4. ALERT DECISION ENGINE ===\n   - Normal: no alert, dashboard stays green\n   - Suspect: in-app/push notification to the doctor currently on duty\n   - Pathological: escalating alert \342\200\224 push + SMS + automated phone \n     call, repeating/escalating to backup if unacknowledged within \n     [X] minutes\n   - Every alert requires acknowledgment, logged with timestamp\n\n=== 5. DUTY ROSTER & ON-CALL ROUTING ===\n   - Simple roster table: doctor name, phone number, ward, shift \n     start/end (manually populated for demo, structured so it could \n     later sync from a real hospital scheduling system)\n   - \"Who\'s on duty now\" lookup: matches current time + ward against \n     roster entries, returns the correct doctor\'s contact info\n   - Fallback chain: if primary on-duty doctor doesn\'t acknowledge, \n     auto-escalate to backup doctor / charge nurse\n   - This lookup result feeds directly into the notification step \n     below \342\200\224 alerts always route to whoever is actually on duty, \n     not a hardcoded contact\n\n=== 6. WARD DASHBOARD ===\n   - Multi-bed view, status color-coded, light theme\n   - Click into a bed opens the dark live waveform monitor panel\n\n=== 7. NOTIFICATION DELIVERY ===\n   - Web Push API via PWA for in-app alerts\n   - Twilio SMS + Voice API for Pathological escalation, called \n     number pulled from the duty roster lookup, not fixed\n   - Do NOT attempt hospital PA/nurse-call integration \342\200\224 out of scope\n\nExplicitly label the system throughout as a clinical decision-support \nprototype, not a deployed medical device. All patient data and duty \nroster entries are simulated for this demo. No real device integration \nin this build.\n\n\n\nHere is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/public/assets/aistudio/.gitignore\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.1.14\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^5.0.4\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^6.2.3\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.1.14\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ~5.8.2\nvite: ^6.2.3\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {StrictMode} from \'react\';\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(\n  <StrictMode>\n    <App />\n  </StrictMode>,\n);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\303\242\302\200\302\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
    items {
      text: "User prompt: Build a real-time CTG monitoring demo system extending the existing \nmodel (models/family_b_gradient_boosting.joblib) and FastAPI backend \n(src/app.py). This is a hackathon prototype simulating a hospital \nworkflow \342\200\224 not a real clinical deployment.\n\n=== DESIGN SYSTEM ===\n\nTwo visual modes in the same app:\n\nA) DASHBOARD SHELL (ward overview, patient list, forms, settings)\n   - Light theme: white/off-white backgrounds (#FAFAFA), soft card \n     shadows, thin borders\n   - Primary accent: royal blue (#0055FF)\n   - Heading text: near-black (#0B0B14), body text: dark gray (#4B4B55)\n   - Fonts: \"Plus Jakarta Sans\" for all UI text and body copy; \n     \"Instrument Serif\" (italic) for hero headings/emphasis words only, \n     matching a serif-italic-accent + clean-sans pairing\n   - Buttons: solid royal blue fill, white text, rounded corners\n\nB) LIVE WAVEFORM MONITOR PANEL (per-patient live view \342\200\224 this is the \n   hero component)\n   - Dark theme, isolated to this panel only: near-black background \n     (#0A0A0F), subtle grid lines like an oscilloscope\n   - Font: monospace throughout (IBM Plex Mono or JetBrains Mono), \n     all-caps labels\n   - FHR (fetal heart rate) trace color changes live with current \n     classification: mint green (#34D399) = Normal, amber (#F5A623) \n     = Suspect, red (#F04438) = Pathological\n   - UC (uterine contraction) trace: fixed violet (#A78BFA), \n     independent of classification\n   - Classification shown as pill badges at top (shield-check icon \n     for Normal, warning-triangle for Suspect, bolt icon for \n     Pathological), active one highlighted in its color\n   - Live readout box: current bpm, ASTV %, and a one-line morphology \n     description (e.g. \"Reduced variability & early decelerations\")\n   - Trace scrolls left-to-right in real time like a live monitor, \n     fed directly from the CTG Data Simulator / feature stream below\n\n=== 1. CTG DATA SIMULATOR ===\n   - Standalone service streaming synthetic FHR + UC signal over \n     WebSocket at realistic sampling rates, feeding both the feature \n     extraction pipeline AND the live waveform panel\'s animation\n   - 3 patient trajectories: stable/Normal, drifting toward Suspect, \n     acute Pathological event\n   - Multiple simultaneous simulated patients/beds\n\n=== 2. FEATURE EXTRACTION SERVICE ===\n   - Rolling window (e.g. 5 min) over the raw stream, computes the \n     21 CTG features the model expects (reference EXPLAINABILITY.md)\n   - Time-constrained fallback allowed: simulate pre-aggregated \n     feature vectors directly, clearly labeled as a scoped shortcut\n\n=== 3. REAL-TIME INFERENCE LOOP ===\n   - Runs the existing model on each new feature vector, per patient, \n     maintains per-patient state/history\n\n=== 4. ALERT DECISION ENGINE ===\n   - Normal: no alert, dashboard stays green\n   - Suspect: in-app/push notification to the doctor currently on duty\n   - Pathological: escalating alert \342\200\224 push + SMS + automated phone \n     call, repeating/escalating to backup if unacknowledged within \n     [X] minutes\n   - Every alert requires acknowledgment, logged with timestamp\n\n=== 5. DUTY ROSTER & ON-CALL ROUTING ===\n   - Simple roster table: doctor name, phone number, ward, shift \n     start/end (manually populated for demo, structured so it could \n     later sync from a real hospital scheduling system)\n   - \"Who\'s on duty now\" lookup: matches current time + ward against \n     roster entries, returns the correct doctor\'s contact info\n   - Fallback chain: if primary on-duty doctor doesn\'t acknowledge, \n     auto-escalate to backup doctor / charge nurse\n   - This lookup result feeds directly into the notification step \n     below \342\200\224 alerts always route to whoever is actually on duty, \n     not a hardcoded contact\n\n=== 6. WARD DASHBOARD ===\n   - Multi-bed view, status color-coded, light theme\n   - Click into a bed opens the dark live waveform monitor panel\n\n=== 7. NOTIFICATION DELIVERY ===\n   - Web Push API via PWA for in-app alerts\n   - Twilio SMS + Voice API for Pathological escalation, called \n     number pulled from the duty roster lookup, not fixed\n   - Do NOT attempt hospital PA/nurse-call integration \342\200\224 out of scope\n\nExplicitly label the system throughout as a clinical decision-support \nprototype, not a deployed medical device. All patient data and duty \nroster entries are simulated for this demo. No real device integration \nin this build.\n\n\n\nHere is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/public/assets/aistudio/.gitignore\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.1.14\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^5.0.4\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^6.2.3\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.1.14\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ~5.8.2\nvite: ^6.2.3\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {StrictMode} from \'react\';\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(\n  <StrictMode>\n    <App />\n  </StrictMode>,\n);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\303\242\302\200\302\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
