      text: "Build a real-time CTG monitoring demo system extending the existing \nmodel (models/family_b_gradient_boosting.joblib) and FastAPI backend \n(src/app.py). This is a hackathon prototype simulating a hospital \nworkflow \342\200\224 not a real clinical deployment.\n\n=== DESIGN SYSTEM ===\n\nTwo visual modes in the same app:\n\nA) DASHBOARD SHELL (ward overview, patient list, forms, settings)\n   - Light theme: white/off-white backgrounds (#FAFAFA), soft card \n     shadows, thin borders\n   - Primary accent: royal blue (#0055FF)\n   - Heading text: near-black (#0B0B14), body text: dark gray (#4B4B55)\n   - Fonts: \"Plus Jakarta Sans\" for all UI text and body copy; \n     \"Instrument Serif\" (italic) for hero headings/emphasis words only, \n     matching a serif-italic-accent + clean-sans pairing\n   - Buttons: solid royal blue fill, white text, rounded corners\n\nB) LIVE WAVEFORM MONITOR PANEL (per-patient live view \342\200\224 this is the \n   hero component)\n   - Dark theme, isolated to this panel only: near-black background \n     (#0A0A0F), subtle grid lines like an oscilloscope\n   - Font: monospace throughout (IBM Plex Mono or JetBrains Mono), \n     all-caps labels\n   - FHR (fetal heart rate) trace color changes live with current \n     classification: mint green (#34D399) = Normal, amber (#F5A623) \n     = Suspect, red (#F04438) = Pathological\n   - UC (uterine contraction) trace: fixed violet (#A78BFA), \n     independent of classification\n   - Classification shown as pill badges at top (shield-check icon \n     for Normal, warning-triangle for Suspect, bolt icon for \n     Pathological), active one highlighted in its color\n   - Live readout box: current bpm, ASTV %, and a one-line morphology \n     description (e.g. \"Reduced variability & early decelerations\")\n   - Trace scrolls left-to-right in real time like a live monitor, \n     fed directly from the CTG Data Simulator / feature stream below\n\n=== 1. CTG DATA SIMULATOR ===\n   - Standalone service streaming synthetic FHR + UC signal over \n     WebSocket at realistic sampling rates, feeding both the feature \n     extraction pipeline AND the live waveform panel\'s animation\n   - 3 patient trajectories: stable/Normal, drifting toward Suspect, \n     acute Pathological event\n   - Multiple simultaneous simulated patients/beds\n\n=== 2. FEATURE EXTRACTION SERVICE ===\n   - Rolling window (e.g. 5 min) over the raw stream, computes the \n     21 CTG features the model expects (reference EXPLAINABILITY.md)\n   - Time-constrained fallback allowed: simulate pre-aggregated \n     feature vectors directly, clearly labeled as a scoped shortcut\n\n=== 3. REAL-TIME INFERENCE LOOP ===\n   - Runs the existing model on each new feature vector, per patient, \n     maintains per-patient state/history\n\n=== 4. ALERT DECISION ENGINE ===\n   - Normal: no alert, dashboard stays green\n   - Suspect: in-app/push notification to the doctor currently on duty\n   - Pathological: escalating alert \342\200\224 push + SMS + automated phone \n     call, repeating/escalating to backup if unacknowledged within \n     [X] minutes\n   - Every alert requires acknowledgment, logged with timestamp\n\n=== 5. DUTY ROSTER & ON-CALL ROUTING ===\n   - Simple roster table: doctor name, phone number, ward, shift \n     start/end (manually populated for demo, structured so it could \n     later sync from a real hospital scheduling system)\n   - \"Who\'s on duty now\" lookup: matches current time + ward against \n     roster entries, returns the correct doctor\'s contact info\n   - Fallback chain: if primary on-duty doctor doesn\'t acknowledge, \n     auto-escalate to backup doctor / charge nurse\n   - This lookup result feeds directly into the notification step \n     below \342\200\224 alerts always route to whoever is actually on duty, \n     not a hardcoded contact\n\n=== 6. WARD DASHBOARD ===\n   - Multi-bed view, status color-coded, light theme\n   - Click into a bed opens the dark live waveform monitor panel\n\n=== 7. NOTIFICATION DELIVERY ===\n   - Web Push API via PWA for in-app alerts\n   - Twilio SMS + Voice API for Pathological escalation, called \n     number pulled from the duty roster lookup, not fixed\n   - Do NOT attempt hospital PA/nurse-call integration \342\200\224 out of scope\n\nExplicitly label the system throughout as a clinical decision-support \nprototype, not a deployed medical device. All patient data and duty \nroster entries are simulated for this demo. No real device integration \nin this build.\n\n"
    }
  }
}
