  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing Design Requirements**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics. I\'m carefully reviewing the user\'s request, especially the design system components and features needed. Right now, I\'m focusing on the dashboard shell, which includes the ward overview, patient list and forms.\n\n\n**Defining Visual Styles**\n\nI\'m now nailing down the visual styles. I\'ve chosen light and dark themes with specific color palettes. I\'ve selected \"Plus Jakarta Sans\" for the main UI text and \"Instrument Serif\" (italic) for hero elements. For the live waveform monitor, I\'m going with a dark theme and monospace fonts. The FHR trace color will dynamically change based on its classification, using mint green for Normal.\n\n\n**Specifying Color Palettes**\n\nI\'m currently finalizing the color specifications. I\'ve defined specific colors for different FHR classifications: amber for Suspect, and red for Pathological. Uterine Contraction (UC) trace will be fixed violet. I\'m also planning the classification badges, using specific icons and colors. Lastly, I\'m integrating a live readout box and audio simulation details.\n\n\n**Analyzing Patient Metrics**\n\nI\'m now analyzing patient metrics, including fetal heart rate and uterine contraction data. I\'m focusing on three specific patient scenarios: normal, drifting toward suspect, and acute pathological. I\'m also considering support for extra beds and customizable patient trajectories. Finally, I need to design speed controls and an event injector for simulation.\n\n\n**Calculating CTG Features**\n\nI am now focusing on data processing, and am building out the functionality to compute CTG standard features. I\'m taking a time slice from the raw data and computing all 21 standard features like baseline, accelerations, decelerations, variability, and histogram data.\n\n\n**Developing Feature Calculations**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the feature calculations, and I\'ve added a detailed feature inspection drawer. This drawer will show the exact formulas, and use SHAP/feature contribution bars for explainability, breaking down each feature. I\'m also now focusing on the real-time inference loop and the alert decision engine.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 128144672
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
