  planner_response {
    response: "I have built the real-time Cardiotocography (CTG) Fetal Telemetry Monitoring and Clinical Decision-Support prototype extending the Gradient Boosting model (`family_b_gradient_boosting.joblib`) and simulated hospital escalation workflow.\n\n### Summary of Implementation\n\n- **Dual-Mode Visual Design System**:\n  - **Light Theme Dashboard Shell (`#FAFAFA`)**: Built with high-contrast typography pairing (*Plus Jakarta Sans* for clean UI and body text, with *Instrument Serif* italic accents for emphasis), royal blue (`#0055FF`) action buttons, and a structured multi-bed ward grid.\n  - **Hero Live Waveform Monitor Panel (`#0A0A0F`)**: An isolated dark-theme oscilloscope interface featuring monospace typography, 50ms / 20bpm grid divisions, and real-time left-to-right scrolling canvas waveforms. The FHR trace dynamically transitions color based on real-time classification\342\200\224**Mint Green** (`#34D399`) for Normal, **Amber** (`#F5A623`) for Suspect, and **Red** (`#F04438`) for Pathological\342\200\224with a fixed **Violet** (`#A78BFA`) trace for uterine contractions (UC/TOCO). Includes live readouts for BPM, ASTV %, and FIGO morphology descriptions.\n\n- **1. Physiological CTG Data Simulator**:\n  - Synthesizes 4 Hz FHR and uterine contraction signals with autonomic beat-to-beat variability (STV & LTV), physiological accelerations, contraction-lagged decelerations, and signal quality metrics.\n  - Pre-configured across 6 obstetrics beds with 3 core trajectories: *Stable Normal*, *Drifting toward Suspect*, and *Acute Pathological Event*, with on-the-fly scenario injection for cord compression, hyperstimulation, prolonged decelerations, and maternal O2 recovery.\n\n- **2. 21 CTG Feature Extraction & SHAP Explainability**:\n  - Rolling sliding-window feature extractor computing all 21 FIGO/UCI benchmark features (`LB`, `AC`, `FM`, `UC`, `DL`, `DS`, `DP`, `ASTV`, `MSTV`, `ALTV`, `MLTV`, `Width`, `Min`, `Max`, `Nmax`, `Nzeros`, `Mode`, `Mean`, `Median`, `Variance`, `Tendency`).\n  - Interactive *What-If* parameter playground and SHAP decision-weight visualizers.\n\n- **3. Real-Time Inference Loop**:\n  - Evaluates decision boundaries replicating `family_b_gradient_boosting.joblib`, returning calibrated softmax probability vectors across Normal, Suspect, and Pathological classes.\n\n- **4. Alert Decision Engine & Clinician Acknowledgment**:\n  - Multi-tier escalation protocol with live countdown timers, requiring physician sign-off, intervention checklists (e.g., maternal tilt, oxytocin cessation, fluid bolus), and audit trail logging.\n\n- **5. Duty Roster & Dynamic On-Call Routing**:\n  - Shift roster table with automated \"Who\'s on duty now\" matching for Ward Unit 4 across Day (07:00\342\200\22319:00) and Night (19:00\342\200\22307:00) shifts.\n  - Auto-escalating fallback chain: Primary Attending $\\rightarrow$ Backup Obstetric Registrar $\\rightarrow$ Charge Midwife / Floor Lead.\n\n- **6. Notification Delivery Hub (Web Push & Twilio SMS/Voice)**:\n  - Web Push API browser notifications for in-app clinical alerts.\n  - Interactive Twilio cellular dispatch terminal featuring a simulated smartphone screen, SMS inbox feed, outbound dispatch audit logs, and playable automated voice synthesized phone calls.\n\n- **Clinical Prototype Notice**:\n  - Prominently displays decision-support research disclaimers indicating that all patient data, waveforms, and roster entries are simulated for demonstration purposes."
    thinking: "**Reviewing Initial Design**\n\nI\'ve just finished reviewing the foundational elements. I\'ve got the dual visual mode design system down, specifically focusing on the dashboard shell. I\'ve set up the light theme with `#FAFAFA`, the royal blue, and chosen specific colors for headings and body text, with Plus Jakarta Sans as the chosen font.\n\n\n"
